{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>How good are your tents.</b> Because he saw that their openings were not aligned one opposite another." "<b>Your dwellings.</b> Your encampments, as the Targum renders. Another matter: <b>How good are your tents</b> — how good were the tent of Shiloh and the eternal House in their habitation, for sacrifices were offered in them to atone for you." "<b>Your dwellings.</b> Even when they are destroyed — for they are a pledge upon you, and their destruction is atonement for the souls, as it says: ״כִּלָּה י׳ אֶת חֲמָתוֹ״ (Lamentations 4) — and with what did He finish? (ibid.) ״וַיַּצֵּת אֵשׁ בְּצִיּוֹן״ (Tanḥuma, Mishpatim)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:32.806934670Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}